# config.local.sh.example - copy this to config.local.sh and edit.
#
# config.local.sh is gitignored and sourced last by config.sh, so anything
# you set here overrides that file's defaults without you ever having to
# edit the tracked config.sh - useful if you're reusing this repo for your
# own setup and want `git pull` to keep working cleanly against upstream.
#
# Only override what you need to change; anything you don't set here keeps
# config.sh's default. See config.sh itself for the full list of variables
# and what each one does.

# GIT_USER_NAME="Your Name"
# GIT_USER_EMAIL="you@example.com"
# GITHUB_ID="your-github-username"
# VM_USER="yourusername"
# UTMCTL="/Applications/UTM.app/Contents/MacOS/utmctl"
